# Routing for the single-page app.
#
# Served by the Cloudflare **Worker** `in-the-vial` using static assets — NOT
# Cloudflare Pages (there is no Pages project on the account). Workers static
# assets read this same _redirects format and do support 200 proxying, which is
# what the rewrites below rely on. Verified against Cloudflare's docs 2026-08-06.
#
# Every page route is listed EXPLICITLY. A catch-all "/* /index.html 200" was
# deliberately not used, for two reasons:
#   1. It risks shadowing the real files this site serves — tracker.json, the
#      self-hosted fonts, robots.txt, sitemap.xml — if asset precedence ever
#      changes underneath us.
#   2. It turns every typo and every dead inbound link into a soft-200 homepage.
#      An honest 404 is better for readers and better for search.
# Adding a page means adding its line here AND to ROUTES in index.html and to
# sitemap.xml. Miss this file and the route works in-app but 404s on refresh.
#
# /api/* is not listed: it is served by the in-the-vial-subscribe Worker, whose
# route runs ahead of the site Worker. Do not add a rule for it.
#
# The rewrite target is "/" and NOT "/index.html". Workers static assets
# canonicalises /index.html with a 307 to /, and a proxy rule inherits that
# redirect — so `/toolkit /index.html 200` shipped as `/toolkit -> 307 -> /`,
# quietly sending every deep link to the homepage. Proxy to "/" instead.
# Verified with `npx wrangler dev --assets=.`, which runs this same rule engine
# locally; plain python3 -m http.server cannot see any of this.

/science        /             200
/bpc-157        /             200
/ghk-cu         /             200
/semaglutide    /             200
/retatrutide    /             200
/ipamorelin     /             200
/toolkit        /             200
/tracker        /             200
/about          /             200
/methodology    /             200
/legal          /             200

# Trailing slashes are redirected, never rewritten. Serving index.html at
# "/toolkit/" would move the document base to /toolkit/, and the relative
# url(fonts/…) and fetch('tracker.json') paths would resolve to /toolkit/fonts/…
# — unstyled type and a silently stale tracker, with nothing in the console.

/science/       /science      301
/bpc-157/       /bpc-157      301
/ghk-cu/        /ghk-cu       301
/semaglutide/   /semaglutide  301
/retatrutide/   /retatrutide  301
/ipamorelin/    /ipamorelin   301
/toolkit/       /toolkit      301
/tracker/       /tracker      301
/about/         /about        301
/methodology/   /methodology  301
/legal/         /legal        301
